WEBVTT

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:02.164
What if the Three Gorges Dam collapsed?

00:00:02.319 --> 00:00:05.629
It sits in central China,
on the mighty Yangtze river.

00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:11.165
It is the largest power station on Earth,
with 22,500 megawatts of power.

00:00:11.175 --> 00:00:13.215
Its wall is more than two kilometres long,

00:00:13.215 --> 00:00:16.885
and holds back a lake about
six hundred kilometres long.

00:00:16.911 --> 00:00:20.881
Below it, the Yangtze runs more than
fifteen hundred kilometres to the sea.

00:00:20.906 --> 00:00:23.616
Roughly four hundred million
people live in its basin.

00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:25.406
Now picture the wall breaking.

00:00:25.462 --> 00:00:28.732
A wall of water would roar
down the valley, past Yichang,

00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:31.352
Wuhan and Nanjing,
all the way to Shanghai.

00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:34.077
But engineers built it
with flood control in mind,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.117
and experts call a collapse
extremely unlikely.

00:00:37.308 --> 00:00:40.198
So the real question is,
how would the world respond?

